# IBM CMS Pipelines reference

When implementing or changing pipeline behavior, treat **CMS/TSO Pipelines Author's Edition** 1.1.11 (document SL26-0018-05) as the semantic authority:

- Local copy: your local copy of the Author's Edition PDF (not included in this repo; typically gitignored under `docs/reference/`)
- Navigational map: `docs/reference/authors-edition-map.md`
- Our decisions vs IBM: private notes repo https://github.com/portable-pipelines/portable-pipelines-notes (`architecture.md` at the repo root). Cloud agents should read it there when they have access.

## Invariants

- Stages never call each other; only `StageCtx` dispatcher services (`read` / `write` / `commit` / `delay` / `short` / `callpipe`).
- Record-oriented (not Unix byte pipes); one record in flight per connection unless a stage buffers.
- Drain-biased dispatcher scheduling.
- Prefer matching Author’s Edition over inventing Unix-pipe shortcuts.
- For features we implement, use **IBM names and semantics** (e.g. REXX write subcommand is `OUTPUT`, not a invented alias).
- Out-of-scope IBM features: omit them; do not rebrand or half-implement under a different name.
- If ambiguous, pick a rule, document it in that notes repo when you have access, and add a regression test.

## Do not

- Invent alternate spellings for IBM pipeline subcommands or stage verbs.
- Commit IBM PDFs to git.
- Paste large verbatim excerpts from IBM manuals into the repo; summarize and cite section topics instead.
